analyze: description, inputSchema -Provide files, +Use it to check a file -a single code -plus language. +the user shares (for example "analyze this file") for security and quality issues before committing. Minimum call: {"code": "<file contents>"}. Add path (e.g. "app/run.py") so the language comes from the extension; without path or language the language is inferred from the content, else python. For several files send files=[{"path", "content"}] instead. severity and format are optional. parameters: -Provide files, or +Send -(language optional, default python). severity and format are +(one file; path and language optional) or files (several). Everything else is +input examples: [{"code": "import subprocess

def run(cmd):
 return subprocess.call(cmd, shell=True)
"}, {"code": "import subprocess

def run(cmd):
 return subprocess.call(cmd, shell=True)
", "path": "app/run.py", "severity": "MEDIUM"}, {"files": [{"content": "import subprocess

def run(cmd):
 return subprocess.call(cmd, shell=True)
", "path": "src/run.py"}]}] -A single +Contents of one file or -only when files is omi compare: description, inputSchema +Use it when the user asks how HefestoAI differs from another scanner. +All arguments are optional: {} compares with sonarqube. parameters: +input examples: [{}, {"tool": "semgrep"}] +Optional. install: description +Use it when the user wants to run HefestoAI locally, in a pre-commit hook or on a whole repository. -parameters. +parameters: call it with {}. pricing: description, outputSchema -PRO: $8/month, OMEGA: +PRO $8/month per user, OMEGA +Use it when the user asks what HefestoAI costs. -parameters. +parameters: call it with {}. parameters: -OMEGA: +OMEGA -PRO: $8/month. +PRO $8/month per user.

sepolia_eth: description, title  -agent +agent, test suite -developer +CI job -test ETH now, without a +gas now: one x402 call, no -address). +address); sends 0.1 SepETH (1 SepETH: /v1/testnet/sepolia-eth/1). -blockNumber, -0.1 SepETH, +amountEth, -to, nonce. Limits +to. Daily limits (UTC): 5 SepETH -UTC day: 1 SepETH (10 calls) per address, +address (both sizes), -overall, plus stock; all +overall;
